<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<resources>
    <!--
      The window background, before the first Compose frame exists.

      Two values and two files: this one is the light theme's `bg-primary`, and `values-night/`
      carries the dark theme's. They are here as well as in `DeckPalette.kt` because a resource is
      the only thing the window manager can read *before* the process has drawn anything, and the
      gap between the window appearing and the first frame landing is exactly where a white flash
      happens.

      They are a fallback, not the decision. `MainActivity.onCreate` reads the stored preference and
      paints the window itself, which is what makes the "Light" choice hold on a phone whose system
      setting is dark. These two only decide the frame before that runs, and on a device where the
      preference is System they are already the right answer.
    -->
    <color name="deck_window">#FFFFFFFF</color>
</resources>
